  "answer": "A balanced chemical equation provides several pieces of information. First, it tells us about the reactants and products involved in the reaction through their symbols and formulae. Second, it shows the ratio of molecules of reactants and products. Third, it gives the relative masses of reactants and products based on their molecular masses. Fourth, if the masses are expressed in grams, the equation also gives the molar ratios of reactants and products. Fifth, if gases are involved, the equation can be used to calculate their volumes at a given temperature and pressure. Lastly, using molar mass and Avogadro’s number, we can calculate the number of molecules and atoms of different substances involved in the reaction.",
